## Live constraints

- `202` cannot precede commit. Publish failure must not change `202` or the receipt.
- Webhook payload keys are not schema-validated. Unused Granot fields may appear or disappear; capture stores the body as evidence.
- `granot-lifecycle-events*` wake-ups are consumed by `api/queues/granot-lifecycle-consumer.ts`, which accepts only `{ receipt_id }` and calls the shared drainer. Five-minute cron `/api/cron/granot-lifecycle-drain` scans due work. Mongo claim/fence selects the single winner.
- Processing disabled means no claim; capture and due work remain intact.
- Processing and shadow default true. All eight effect flags stay false.
- Shadow, retry, and requeue must not create, update, cancel, or un-cancel a Booking.
- Capture, identity, and planner have no production Lead/Booking/Cancellation write path. Matched-Lead field writes exist only through `synchronizeLeadFromGranot` when live + Lead writes + all eight gates authorize them. Authorized create-if-missing writes exist only through `createLeadFromGranot` when live + Lead creation + all eight creation gates authorize them **and** `route_event_class` is `lead_created` (any selected model). `priority_updated`, `link_only`, and `booking_status_changed` never mint. `requested_effect` stays `"lead_created"`; there is no ninth gate; do not change `sourcePolicy.ts` or `leadMessaging/`. Checked-in defaults keep shadow true and Lead writes/creation false. Unit 19 does not enable Registry `create_if_missing` or change indexes.
- When a Call Observation has a phone, both Granot lock sites always run; [RingCentral Call Adoption](../../../CONTEXT.md) mutations and the ingest lock stay flagged — do not describe the ingest lock as always on. Owner language uses [Caller Match Key](../../../CONTEXT.md); the locked implementation key is exact Source Granularity + normalized phone — never Source Company alone. A later inbound Observation for the same Job or the same exact key **synchronizes**. Call Qualification remains the Call Lead qualifier for mapped inbound streams. Best Relocation Forms and Inbounds keep `create_if_missing`. Residual holes, inbound-family `link_only` posture, and Best Relocation SMS stay in [processor](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/processor.md), [source-policy](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/source-policy.md), [call-lead](../../docs/knowledge/services/call-lead.md), and [lifecycle-activation-flags-and-source-policies.md](../../docs/granot-lead-lifecycle/lifecycle-activation-flags-and-source-policies.md). Do not paper holes over, do not say Main Site / 10best / TBM Prime / Top10 Inbounds are `create_if_missing`, and do not enable `outbound_sms` from this map.
